{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A planar embedding of a graph: a rotation system, the clockwise order of the edges around each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, over every edge position (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PlanarEmbedding"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PlanarEmbedding"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"OGDF’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CombinatorialEmbedding"},{"type":"text","text":"). Its faces satisfy Euler’s formula, n − m + f = 2, in every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected component with an edge."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/planarity\/planarembedding"]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PlanarEmbedding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A self-loop appears twice in its vertex’s order, its two ends adjacent, enclosing a face of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length 1. Parallel copies sit side by side, each consecutive pair enclosing a face of length 2.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each clockwise order starts at the first edge of ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Faces."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The face after the half-edge from u along edge e to w continues with the half-edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before e in the clockwise order at w (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next_face_half_edge"},{"type":"text","text":"), so a face lies to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right of each of its half-edges. Faces are counted per connected component, and an isolated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex has none: two disjoint triangles have four faces."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The embedding keeps the graph it was made from (copy-on-write, so O(1)); mutating the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"afterwards does not change it. When a graph has several embeddings, which one is returned is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not specified, but it depends only on the graph’s rows: graphs with the same vertices, the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge positions and the same incidence order get the same embedding."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/ClockwiseInc